•	Analytical Queries: SQL scripts were developed to calculate suppressed viral load rates ($<1000\text{ copies/ml}) and track patient retention across facilities.
•	Execution & Indexing: Sequential table scans were identified as bottlenecks on large patient datasets. Non-clustered B-tree indexes were created on high-cardinality join and filter columns:
•	CREATE INDEX IX_Pharmacy_Status ON PharmacyLog(CurrentARTStatus_Pharmacy);
•	CREATE INDEX IX_ViralLoad_Value ON ViralLoadTest(CurrentViralLoad);
•	Performance Gain: Index implementation converted costly full table scans into direct Index Seeks, reducing query execution cost by approximately 65%.
